<?php

namespace Illuminate\Support\Facades;

/**
 * Laravel declares a narrower `@method static bool hasTable(string $table)` on the
 * facade. The concrete method below both widens that parameter and carries the taint sink.
 *
 * FacadeStubPrecedenceHandler removes the shadowing vendor pseudo-method after population,
 * so native resolution consults this concrete stub for both type and taint metadata.
 *
 * Runtime: Builder::hasTable string-concatenates the table prefix with `$table`, which
 * coerces any stringable object via __toString.
 *
 * Every other Schema\Builder method resolves through the `@mixin` below, not the facade's generated
 * `@method` tags: Psalm consults a mixin target's real method before the facade's pseudo-static
 * entries, so the introspection methods get the types of the Builder stub
 * (stubs/common/Database/Schema/Builder.phpstub), which corrects Laravel's docblocks where they contradict
 * the driver processors, instead of the tags' bare `array`. `Schema::connection()->...` instance calls
 * share those types.
 *
 * The mixin also brings Builder's PARAM types, which are narrower than the facade tags for the column
 * lists (`array<string>` vs `array`). The methods declared below restate the facade tags verbatim so
 * calls that were accepted before the mixin (an Expression or Stringable in the list, both handled at
 * runtime) stay accepted. `defaultStringLength(non-negative-int)` is deliberately NOT restated: a
 * negative length is not validated by the method itself and fails later, when the DDL for a string column is built.
 *
 * @mixin \Illuminate\Database\Schema\Builder
 */
class Schema extends Facade
{
    /**
     * @param  string|\Stringable  $table
     * @return bool
     *
     * @psalm-taint-sink sql $table
     */
    public static function hasTable($table) {}

    /**
     * @param  string  $table
     * @param  array  $columns
     * @return bool
     */
    public static function hasColumns($table, $columns) {}

    /**
     * @param  string  $table
     * @param  string|array  $columns
     * @return void
     */
    public static function dropColumns($table, $columns) {}
}
